        "text": "def solve(rows):\n    \"\"\"Solves the interval merging problem according to the given rules.\n\n    Args:\n        rows: A list of integer half-open intervals.\n\n    Returns:\n        A sorted list of merged integer half-open intervals.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    # Audit filter: Omit positions whose index modulo 4 equals 1, except always retain the last position.\n    filtered_rows = []\n    for i, interval in enumerate(rows):\n        if i % 4 != 1 or i == len(rows) - 1:\n            filtered_rows.append(interval)\n\n    # Rotate the retained rows left by 3 positions modulo the retained length.\n    rotated_rows = []\n    for interval in filtered_rows:\n        start, end = interval\n        length = end - start + 1\n        rotate_amount = (start - 3) % length\n        rotated_start = start + rotate_amount\n        rotated_end = rotated_start + (end - start) - 1\n        rotated_rows.append((rotated_start, rotated_end))\n\n    # Apply the rules to that transformed list: Rows [start,end] are integer half-open intervals.\n    # Discard empty or reversed intervals.\n    valid_intervals = []\n    for start, end in rotated_rows:\n        if start <= end and start <= end:\n            valid_intervals.append((start, end))\n\n    # Merge overlapping intervals, but do not merge intervals that only touch.\n    merged_intervals = []\n    valid_intervals.sort()\n    i = 0\n    while i < len(valid_intervals):\n        current_start, current_end = valid_intervals[i]\n        j = i + 1\n        while j < len(valid_intervals) and \n               valid_intervals[j][0] <= current_end + 1:\n            current_end = max(current_end, valid_intervals[j][1])\n            j += 1\n        merged_intervals.append((current_start, current_end))\n        i = j\n\n    # Return the requested value, without printing.\n    return sorted(merged_intervals)",
